    "context": "Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to agree who will help whom after a change of circumstances.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U6-03-skill-K-HSK6-pragmatics-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "HSK 6: pragmatics",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "An explicit commitment, a request and an inferred obligation carry different force. Seek the relevant context before assigning an unstated duty; keep the source wording and your inference separate.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "承诺",
                "pinyin": "chéngnuò",
                "meaning": "to promise; to undertake to do something",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "6d2cdf4e5a70f01b38a79b995533ab08da0587a3b3084aefc8244d16d37ead15"
              },
              {
                "text": "委托",
                "pinyin": "wěituō",
                "meaning": "to entrust; to trust",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "23709a51ff56ca03046dac01f66eb90fcafc53baff7c6b526ca855ad0de38302"
              },
              {
                "text": "场合",
                "pinyin": "chǎnghé",
                "meaning": "occasion; setting",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "54dc6e85e526b298b83e398410753c3f4b75d9896e64d879a022771c1f591d94"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A companion requests help today and assumes an earlier promise guarantees it. The actual promise was to help tomorrow, with no task specified. No one has accepted today’s request. Ask what task is intended, distinguish that request from the limited promise, and avoid inventing a duty today.\nFamiliar meanings available: to promise; to undertake to do something; to entrust; to trust; occasion; setting."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U6-03-skill-K-HSK6-pragmatics-perform",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Use the skill in context",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U6-03-skill-K-HSK6-pragmatics-perform",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "spoken",
            "prompt": "Interpret the familiar request and commitment. Ask for the missing context before claiming that someone is obliged to act, then give a suitable response.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "A companion requests help today and assumes an earlier promise guarantees it. The actual promise was to help tomorrow, with no task specified. No one has accepted today’s request. Ask what task is intended, distinguish that request from the limited promise, and avoid inventing a duty today.\nFamiliar meanings available: to promise; to undertake to do something; to entrust; to trust; occasion; setting.",
            "contextLanguage": "en",
            "label": "Take your speaking turn",
            "resultDomain": "Self-reviewed speaking practice",
            "rubric": [
              {
                "id": "r1",
                "text": "I distinguished explicit commitment from inferred obligation."
              },
              {
                "id": "r2",
                "text": "My response seeks missing context and preserves the source’s qualification."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "sequential": true
      }
